For self-hosted users, get a dedicated physical connection corresponding to the given ID. The response object includes information such as the connection's name, status and total bandwidth.

USAGE:
  scw interlink connection get <connection-id ...> [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  connection-id     ID of connection to get
  [region=fr-par]   Region to target. If none is passed will use default region from the config (fr-par | it-mil | nl-ams | pl-waw)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for get
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers       Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
